age?url=%2Fimages%2FGyucnnqW8AA_tBY.jpg&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FGyucnnqW8AA_tBY.jpg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FGyucnnqW8AA_tBY.jpg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FGyucnnqW8AA_tBY.jpg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FGyucnnqW8AA_tBY.jpg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FGyucnnqW8AA_tBY.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FGyucnnqW8AA_tBY.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/><div class="cap"><h4>Health Committee members at the Assembly — the accountability chain, in the room.</h4><div class="meta">Ommi activity 05 · Garissa</div></div></div><div class="fn-slide"><span class="frame">Frame <!-- -->04<!-- --> /<!-- --> <!-- -->04</span><img alt="A fruitful discussion on reducing maternal and child mortality" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" sizes="60vw" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FGyucnvYWIAAEYoL.jpg&amp;w=384&amp;q=75 384w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FGyucnvYWIAAEYoL.jpg&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FGyucnvYWIAAEYoL.jpg&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FGyucnvYWIAAEYoL.jpg&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FGyucnvYWIAAEYoL.jpg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FGyucnvYWIAAEYoL.jpg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FGyucnvYWIAAEYoL.jpg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FGyucnvYWIAAEYoL.jpg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FGyucnvYWIAAEYoL.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FGyucnvYWIAAEYoL.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/><div class="cap"><h4>A fruitful discussion, deliberations agreed upon — the field note of a working meeting.</h4><div class="meta">Ommi activity 05 · Garissa</div></div></div></div><div class="fn-dots" role="tablist" aria-label="Story slides"><button class="on" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-label="Go to frame 1"></button><button class="" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-label="Go to frame 2"></button><button class="" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-label="Go to frame 3"></button><button class="" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-label="Go to frame 4"></button></div><div class="fn-nav"><button class="arrow" aria-label="Previous frame"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 18l-6-6 6-6"></path></svg></button><button class="arrow" aria-label="Next frame"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"></path></svg></button></div></div><div class="rv fn-side"><div class="fn-card"><div class="no">— The story —</div><h3>Who was in the room.</h3><p>We sat with the people responsible for Garissa’s maternal and newborn health: the<!-- --> <strong style="color:#fff">CECM Health, the Chief Officer, the Director for Health</strong>, the <strong style="color:#fff">Health Committee</strong> <!-- -->at the Assembly, and the<!-- --> <strong style="color:#fff">Budget Committee members</strong>.</p><p>Health leadership and money leadership, at one table — because a mother’s survival depends on both.</p><div class="fn-meta"><div><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="18" rx="2"></rect><path d="M16 2v4M8 2v4M3 10h18"></path></svg><span>Tuesday, <b class="bold">19 August 2025</b></span></div><div><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21s-7-5.5-7-11a7 7 0 1 1 14 0c0 5.5-7 11-7 11Z"></path><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="2.6"></circle></svg><span><b class="bold">Garissa County</b>, North Eastern Kenya</span></div><div><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"></path><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"></circle><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"></path></svg><span>CECM Health · Chief Officer · Director of Health · Assembly Health &amp; Budget Committees</span></div></div></div><div class="verify-note"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"></path></svg><span><b>Note for the team:</b> captions are drawn from @Fountain_FOH’s post (19 Aug 2025) and the OMMI Year 1 report. Confirm photo-to-person attribution against the originals before publishing.</span></div></div></div></div></section><section class="discuss" id="discuss"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv discuss-nav"><span class="eyebrow eyebrow--paper">The discussion, unpacked</span><h2>What the room <em>agreed.</em></h2><p>Where the fifth activity sits in the Okoa Mama na Mtoto Year One, and why a budget meeting is a life-saving meeting.</p></div><div class="rv discuss-body"><div class="dd-block"><h3><span class="num">01</span> Why a budget meeting</h3><p>Maternal and newborn deaths are not only a health story — they are a <strong>money story</strong>. A mother’s survival depends on staffed facilities, equipped referral and emergency transport, all of which rest on county budget decisions. The fifth activity took the Okoa Mama na Mtoto conversation to the people who write those budgets: the<!-- --> <strong>Health Committee</strong> and the<!-- --> <strong>Budget Committee</strong> at the County Assembly, with the county’s health executive at the table.</p><p>Bringing health leadership and money leadership together into one deliberation is the entire argument of this field note —<!-- --> <strong>the money must follow the mother</strong>.</p></div><div class="dd-block"><h3><span class="num">02</span> What was on the table</h3><p>The working meeting opened with the data and realities of the Okoa Mama na Mtoto landscape, then moved to the decisions the county can make with, and for, its mothers.</p><div class="dd-facts"><div class="fact"><div class="k">The budget gap</div><div class="v">A county health budget under pressure leaves too little for the <b>commodities, referral and facilities</b> that save mothers — the very conversation this meeting opened.</div></div><div class="fact"><div class="k">The referral chain</div><div class="v"><b>Cross-county referrals</b> and emergency transport are a lifeline, yet remain one of the weakest links between a mother, a facility and a skilled birth attendant.</div></div><div class="fact"><div class="k">The agreement</div><div class="v">Fruitful deliberation, and a commitment the room<!-- --> <b>agreed upon together</b> — carried from the table into the county’s next budget and policy conversations.</div></div></div></div><div class="dd-quote"><span class="qmark">“</span><blockquote>On to the 5th activity … A fruitful discussion, and deliberations we agreed upon together.</blockquote><div class="who">Fountain of Hope · Okoa Mama na Mtoto, on X</div></div><div class="dd-block"><h3><span class="num">03</span> Where this sits in a year of advocacy</h3><p>This was not a one-off meeting. It is the fifth activity in a deliberately sequenced year of maternal and newborn health advocacy in Garissa — from county health landscaping, through the women’s faith network and youth champions, into the rooms where resource decisions are made. The topic pages on this site tell the wider story of the whole initiative.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="related" id="related"><div class="wrap"><div class="rel-head rv"><div><span class="eyebrow eyebrow--paper">Keep exploring</span><h2 class="h2">More topics from <em>the field.</em></h2></div></div><div class="rel-grid"><a class="rel rv" href="/topics/menstrual-health"><div class="rel-num">→ <!-- -->Topic 02</div><h4>Why a girl in Garissa should never miss school because she cannot afford a pad</h4><p>Menstrual health support, dignity kits and school advocacy that keep Garissa’s girls learning.</p><span class="lnk">Read the story<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a><a class="rel rv" href="/topics/clean-water"><div class="rel-num">→ <!-- -->Topic 03</div><h4>Clean water, and the dignity it brings</h4><p>Water, sanitation and hygiene work that protects mothers, children and whole communities in one of Kenya’s driest counties.</p><span class="lnk">Read the story<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a><a class="rel rv" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:var(--navy);border-color:var(--navy)" href="/"><div class="rel-num" style="color:#FF9CBE">All topics</div><h4 style="color:#fff">Back to the Fountain of Hope story</h4><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,.7)">Explore the full one-page story and every topic.</p><span class="lnk" style="color:#FF9CBE;margin-top:auto">Open the home page<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a></div></div></section><section class="cta"><div class="rv cta-in"><span class="eyebrow">Support the work</span><h2>Stand with the women who <em>lead this change.</em></h2><p>Every meeting, every radio message, every faith gathering is a step toward the day no mother or child is left behind.</p><div class="ctas"><a class="btn btn--pink" href="/#footer">Donate now<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20c-3.5-2.6-6-5.6-6-8.5C6 8.6 8.2 7 10 7c1.3 0 2 .8 2 .8S13.7 7 15 7c1.8 0 4 1.6 4 4.5 0 2.9-2.5 5.9-6 8.5Z"></path></svg></a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/#footer">Partner with us</a></div></div></section></main><footer id="footer"><div class="wrap"><div class="foot-grid"><div class="foot-about"><a class="brand" href="/#top"><span class="mark" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20c-3.5-2.6-6-5.6-6-8.5C6 8.6 8.2 7 10 7c1.3 0 2 .8 2 .8S13.7 7 15 7c1.8 0 4 1.6 4 4.5 0 2.9-2.5 5.9-6 8.5Z"></path><path d="M12 6.5v-2M9.5 4.5h5"></path></svg></span><span><span class="name">Fountain of Hope</span><span class="sub">Garissa, Kenya</span></span></a><p>A woman-led community organization working beside the people of Garissa in health, education, clean water and community resilience — because real change is built from within.</p></div><div class="foot-col"><h5>Topics</h5><ul><li><a href="/topics/okoamama-activity-05">Okoa Mama · Budget meeting</a></li><li><a href="/topics/menstrual-health">Girls &amp; education</a></li><li><a href="/topics/clean-water">Clean water</a></li><li><a href="/topics/womens-award">Women’s health award</a></li></ul></div><div class="foot-col"><h5>Get involved</h5><ul><li><a href="/#footer">Donate</a></li><li><a href="/#footer">Partner with us</a></li><li><a href="/#footer">Sponsorship</a></li><li><a href="/#footer">Volunteer</a></li></ul></div><div class="foot-col"><h5>Contact</h5><div class="foot-contact"><div><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" strok